te a & &2 on Ba be a (ea \n(If known). , s i dhe ee Rade oi. Ai \nNature of lJocument. \n(Communist or Anti-Government etc). | she vit % “tin RhheOe “eee Sx \nArrests or not, if so how many ? | = Ean \nClass of man arrested ? (Student, coolie, Can \nmill worker ete.) \nCharged under what Section of C.C, Code? PS \nSigned \nD9): 1 | Mo ES Aa for C. L, etce tfc. tse ty: ths Station.","pages":[{"n":0,"en":"S.C.S.\nSHANGHAI MUNICIPAL POLICE.    File No. ......\nSection 2, Special Branch Station.\nREPORT\nDate 13th November 1935.\nSubject Communist propaganda found in the Dong Shing (同興) Cotton\nMill, 1433 Gordon Road (Pootoo Road District).\nMade by T.S.I. Shih Ssu-chien. Forwarded by [签名]\n\nAttached herewith are two communist handbills which were\ndelivered through the post addressed to Wong Ping H-sing (王炳星),\nDong Shing (同興) Cotton Mill, 1433 Gordon Road. As there is\nno one answering to this name employed with the mill it is\nsurmised that the name is a fictitious one. Enquiries made at\npost offices by detectives attached to Pootoo Road Station and\nSpecial Branch have, however, failed to ascertain the place where\nthe literature was posted as the postal cancellation mark is\nillegible. A summarized translation of the pamphlets is as\nfollows:-\n(1). \"Labourer's Weekly News (工人週刊)\", issue No1, dated\n5/10/35, purporting to have been issued by the \"Labourers Press\",\ncontaining articles dealing with the following:-\n(a). A fresh attack on China by the Japanese Imperialists\nwho are endeavouring to create a \"Second Manchuokuo\" in North\nChina. In this article the people are urged to kill all traitors\nand members of the Kuomintang and to drive the Japanese Imperialists\nout of China;\n(b). General mobilization declared by Abyssinian Government\nto resist the Italian invasion; and that 1,250,000 Abyssinian\nsoldiers have been sent to the front;\n(c). Victories of Soviet Red Armies in Kansu, Western Hunan\nand Western Hupeh;\n(d). Anti-Fascist movement in France;\n(e). War is imminent in the Mediterranean as both Great\nBritain and Italy have mobilised battleships, aeroplanes and\nsubmarines in that region;\n(f). A number of Japanese soldiers killed in Mukden as a\nresult of an attack launched on them by volunteers.\n\n（左侧手写批注：）\n$2,\nFor\ninquiry\nregarding\nsource of\nhandbills\nand report\nplease.\n[签名]\n2 Nov 1935\nD.I. Kuh.\n[签名]\n20/11\nNoted\nKuh 20/11","zh":"S.C.S.\n上海公共租界工部局警务处。 档案号 ......\n特二科（特别支部）巡捕房。\n报告\n日期：1935年11月13日。\n事由：在戈登路（普陀路区）1433号同兴棉纱厂发现共产主义宣传品。\n具报人：T.S.I. 施四鉴。 转呈人：[签名]\n\n随函附上两份共产主义传单，系通过邮政寄往戈登路1433号同兴棉纱厂王炳星（Wong Ping H-sing）收。因该厂并无以此姓名受雇之人员，故推测该姓名为虚构。经隶属于普陀路巡捕房及特科的侦探向各邮局查询，惟因邮戳模糊不清，未能查明该宣传品的投寄地点。传单内容摘要翻译如下：-\n(1). 《工人周刊》，第1期，日期为1935年10月5日，声称由“劳工出版社”发行，包含涉及以下内容的文章：-\n(a). 日本帝国主义者正企图在华北制造“第二个满洲国”，从而对中国发动新的攻击。在该文章中，呼吁民众杀死所有汉奸及国民党成员，并将日本帝国主义者驱逐出中国；\n(b). 阿比西尼亚政府宣布总动员以抵抗意大利入侵；并称已有1,250,000名阿比西尼亚士兵被派往前线；\n(c). 苏联红军在甘肃、湘西及鄂西取得胜利；\n(d). 法国的反法西斯运动；\n(e). 地中海战争迫在眉睫，因英国和意大利均已在该地区动员战舰、飞机及潜艇；\n(f). 多名日本士兵在沈阳因遭到志愿者袭击而丧生。\n\n（左侧手写批注：）\n$2,\n请就\n传单来源\n进行调查\n并具报。\n[签名]\n1935年11月2日\nD.I. Kuh.\n[签名]\n11/20\n已阅\nKuh 11/20"},{"n":1,"en":"SHANGHAI MUNICIPAL POLICE.\nFile No.\nStation,\nREPORT\nDate 19\n-2-\nSubject\nMade by Forwarded by\n\n(2). \"Labourer's Weekly\", issue No.2, dated 12/10/35,\ncontaining the following articles:-\n(a). The Kuomintang is the advance guard of the\nJapanese Imperialists in attacking the Soviet Armies in North\nWest China;\n(b). The International Anti-war movement is working at\nhigh pressure to stop the impending 2nd world war;\n(c). Gas bombs have been dropped in Abyssinia by\nItalian planes;\n(d). The wages of workers in Japanese cotton mills in\nShanghai have been reduced considerably;\n(e). The Japanese Imperialists are planning to attack\nthe U.S.S.R. by taking advantage of the unsettled conditions\nprevailing in Europe.\n\nD. S. I.\n\nC. D. J. Grubb,\nPlease send copy with spare copies\nof handbills to S.P.O. and arrange to\nhave a summary made of the information\nin this report for inclusion in Daily Report.\nCopy of report sent to S.P.O.\nW.G.\n19 NOV. 1935\n11/G. 35\n\nDeputy Commissioner, Special Branch.\n\nD.I. Kuh\nSBR\n19/11\nIncluded in\nS.R. 7 20/11\nKuh","zh":"上海公共租界工部局警务处。\n档案号\n巡捕房，\n报告\n日期 19\n-2-\n事由\n具报人 转呈人\n\n(2). 《工人周刊》，第2期，日期为1935年10月12日，包含以下文章：-\n(a). 国民党是日本帝国主义者在中国西北进攻苏联军队的先锋；\n(b). 国际反战运动正在全力运作，以阻止即将爆发的第二次世界大战；\n(c). 意大利飞机在阿比西尼亚投掷了毒气弹；\n(d). 上海日本棉纱厂工人的工资大幅降低；\n(e). 日本帝国主义者正计划利用欧洲 prevailing 的不稳定局势进攻苏联。\n\nD. S. I.\n\nC. D. J. Grubb,\n请将本报告副本连同传单备用副本送交特别警务处（S.P.O.），并安排将本报告中的信息摘要编入《每日报告》。\n报告副本已送交特别警务处（S.P.O.）。\nW.G.\n1935年11月19日\n11/G. 35\n\n副总监，特科。\n\nD.I. Kuh\nSBR\n11/19\n已编入\nS.R. 7 11/20\nKuh"},{"n":2,"en":"TM 2\nG 40.00U 1.35\n\nMiso. File No. 144/35.\nSHANGHAI MUNICIPAL POLICE.\nPootoo Road Station,\nREPORT\nDate. 16.11.35. 19\nSubject Communist Papers found in the Letter Box of Dong Shing Cotton Mill,\n1433 Gordon Road.\nMade by D.S.I. Hutton. Forwarded by Wmartins S.I\n\nSir,\nI beg to report that 2 papers of an Anti-Japanese and\ncommunistic nature were delived at the Dong Shing Cotton Mill,\n1433 Gordon Road. From enquiries made by S.I. Koga, it was\nascertained that at 5 p.m. 15.11.35, a mill foreman named Mr.\nHashimoto collected the letters from the mill mail box and found\na package addressed to one named Wong Ping Maing (王炳明).\nIt was ascertained that no such person was known at the mill and\nMr. Hashimoto opened the package and found it to contain the 2\nenclosed copies of the Labourers Weekly Publication. The\npapers were handed over to S.I. Koga at 9 a.m. 16.11.35.\nDetectives were sent to the Post office but the post mark could\nnot be traced.\n\nW Hutton\nD.S.I.\n\nD.D.O. \"B\" Division.\nCopies to:- D.I. Kirk\nD.C. (Special Branch) O Martin\nS. P. O. SBR 17/11\n\nFiled\nKirk\n17/11","zh":"TM 2\nG 40.00U 1.35\n\n杂项档案号 144/35。\n上海公共租界工部局警务处。\n普陀路捕房，\n报告\n日期：1935年11月16日。19\n事由：在戈登路1433号东兴纱厂信箱内发现共产主义宣传品。\n呈报人：副巡官赫顿（Hutton）。由警司马丁斯（Wmartins）转呈\n\n敬启者：\n谨此报告，有两份具有反日及共产主义性质的宣传品被投递至戈登路1433号东兴纱厂。经警司古贺（Koga）查询查明，1935年11月15日下午5时，一名名为桥本（Hashimoto）先生的工厂领班从工厂信箱收取信件时，发现一个寄给名为王炳明（Wong Ping Maing）者的包裹。经查，厂内并无此人，桥本先生遂打开包裹，发现内附两份《劳工周刊》（Labourers Weekly Publication）。该两份宣传品已于1935年11月16日上午9时移交警司古贺。探员曾前往邮局调查，但无法追溯邮戳来源。\n\nW 赫顿\n副巡官\n\n“B”区副总监。\n副本致：- 督察长柯克（Kirk）\n特别处助理总监 O 马丁（O Martin）\n特别处警官 SBR 17/11\n\n归档\n柯克\n11月17日"},{"n":3,"en":"F. 489 Inst. 12-31.\n500-12-34.\n\nReport sent with\nSpecial Branch.\npamphlets, handbills or newspapers to\n\nWhere found\nTime found\nDate\n\nCharacter of place where found, (industrial,\nresidential, respectable or doubtful\nneighbourhood).\n\nNear School, Factory, Military Camp, Mill\netc.\n\nHow distributed ?\n(If known)\n\nNature of Document.\n(Communist or Anti-Government etc).\n\nArrests or not, if so how many ?\n\nClass of man arrested ? (Student, coolie,\nmill worker etc.)\n\nCharged under what Section of C.C. Code?\n\n（批：The pamphlet circulated for distribution in Com. area）\n（批：Similar to pamphlet sent thro' post by Shing Hui）\n（批：27/11）\n\nDate 1/1/\nCopy sent to S.P.G.\n\nSigned W. P. C. S.\nfor C. I. etc. at 9. Rd. Station.","zh":"F. 489 指令 12-31。\n500-12-34。\n\n随特别处报告附上\n小册子、传单或报纸至\n\n发现地点\n发现时间\n日期\n\n发现地点的性质（工业区、住宅区、体面街区或可疑街区）。\n\n靠近学校、工厂、军营、纱厂等。\n\n分发方式？\n（如已知）\n\n文件性质。\n（共产主义或反政府等）。\n\n是否逮捕，如是，人数多少？\n\n被捕者身份类别？（学生、苦力、纱厂工人等。）\n\n依据《刑事法典》哪一条款起诉？\n\n（批注：该小册子在共产党活动区域流通分发）\n（批注：与经由邮政寄送的盛辉（Shing Hui）小册子类似）\n（批注：11月27日）\n\n日期 1月1日/\n副本送交特别处总巡官（S.P.G.）。\n\n签名 W. P. C. S.\n代表第九捕房刑事情报股等人员。"},{"n":4,"en":"F. 459 Inst. 12-31.\n1000-2-33.\n\nReport sent with\nSpecial Branch.\npamphlets, handbills or newspapers to\n\n| Where found | Time found | Date |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Character of place where found, (industrial, residential, respectable or doubtful neighbourhood). | | |\n| Near School. Factory, Military Camp, Mill etc. | | |\n| How distributed ? (If known). | | |\n| Nature of Document. (Communist or Anti-Government etc). | | |\n| Arrests or not, if so how many ? | | |\n| Class of man arrested ? (Student, coolie, mill worker etc.) | | |\n|